    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-003",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Finding a Job",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Elena and Clare are each working on a project about how high school students are having trouble finding jobs. They each find the proportion of students without jobs from a random sample, then use a computer to do 1,000 simulations using…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-004",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Finding a Job",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Elena says, “The proportion of high school students without jobs is about 0.70 with a margin of error of 0.280.”",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-005",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Finding a Job",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Clare says, “The proportion of high school students without jobs is about 0.74 with a margin of error of 0.138.”",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-006",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Finding a Job",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Both students reported the margin of error based on 2 standard deviations from their simulations. What are the mean and standard deviation each student found? For at least one student, show your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-007",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Finding a Job",
      "SourceExcerpt": "First they consider the proportion they used in the simulations. Elena says, “My simulation used 0.7 as the proportion since I found that proportion in my original sample.” Clare says, “My simulation used 0.75 as the proportion since I…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-008",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Finding a Job",
      "SourceExcerpt": "They look for more differences in their initial sample and discover than Elena surveyed 10 people in her initial sample and Clare surveyed 40 people. Do you think this is why Clare has a smaller margin of error? Explain your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-009",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Finding a Job",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Clare and Elena try to figure out why Clare had such a smaller range of values in her report.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-010",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Exercised",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Cut a sheet of paper into enough slips for each student in the class to get one. On each of the slips you cut, write “Yes” if you spend at least 5 hours intentionally exercising each week, otherwise write “No” on each of the slips. Put one…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-011",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Exercised",
      "SourceExcerpt": "After all the slips are distributed for all the students, return to your bag. Your teacher gave your group a number of slips to draw for each sample. Draw a sample and record the proportion of the slips that say “Yes.” Return the slips to…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-012",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Exercised",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Use your 50 sample proportions to report an estimate and associated margin of error for the class. Explain or show your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Exercised",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Compare the standard deviations of the 50 sample proportions for each of the different groups. Is there a connection to the number of slips chosen in each sample?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Exercised",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Here is a table of standard deviations that were obtained when repeatedly sampling from a population where the proportion of “Yes” slips was 0.4.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Exercised",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Estimate the standard deviation for a sample size of 500.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Exercised",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Estimating a population characteristic from a random sample will always have some room for error since the sample is only a subset of the population, so it does not provide complete information about the population. One way to reduce the…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Exercised",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For example, a group goes to an island and collects a random sample of 10 lizards, finding that 5 of them are male. This random sample has a proportion of 0.5 males in the group. How close is this likely to be to the actual proportion of…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Exercised",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Suppose we simulate taking 30 random samples of 10 lizards from a population with a 0.5 probability of each one being male, and this results in sample proportions that have a mean of 0.503 and a standard deviation of 0.145. The dot plot of…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Exercised",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Based on the simulations and analysis, we expect that the original estimate of 0.5 for the proportion of the population that is male is likely to be within 0.290 of the actual value of the population proportion of lizards that are male.…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Exercised",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Later, another group goes to the island and collects a sample of 40 lizards, finding that 20 of them are male. After simulating 30 samples of 40 lizards with a 0.5 probability of each one being male, the mean proportion that is male is…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Exercised",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Although the means are the same in this case, the standard deviation is much less with the larger samples, so the margin of error reported was smaller.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L11-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Exercised",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The maximum expected difference between an estimate for a population characteristic and the actual value of the population characteristic.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
